/-! # Relative finite presentation with a finitely presented ambient algebra

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 08KP, hypotheses (1)-(3), in Situations 08KH and 08KK
(blueprint: lem-sfb-relative-fp-module-fp-algebra-pushout).

The ambient algebra factors through a flat algebra followed by a finitely presented
algebra. The overlap modules are expressed by extension from the component algebras,
canonically equivalent to extension from the component base rings.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe uA uA' uB uD uE uN uM

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Module

/-- Relative finite presentation of a patched module, Stacks Project, Tag 08KP,
hypotheses (1)-(3), in Situations 08KH and 08KK
(blueprint: lem-sfb-relative-fp-module-fp-algebra-pushout).

The displayed algebra-map equations fix the pullback projections and the base-change
maps. The scalar towers express restriction of the given actions. The overlap
`D_A ⊗[D_B] N` is canonically `N ⊗[B] A`, and similarly on the primed side.
The kernel of the difference consists of the compatible pairs, with the inherited
coordinatewise `D`-action. No flatness of `D` over the pullback ring is assumed.

Proof plan:
1. Choose a surjection `P = E[x₁, ..., xₙ] → D` with kernel generated by finitely
   many elements, using `def-weil-pbc-finitely-presented-algebra`. Monomials form
   an `E`-basis (`def-weil-pbc-mv-polynomial-ring`), so `P` is flat over `E`
   (`lem-weil-pbc-projective-module-flat`) and hence over the pullback ring
   (`lem-pc-module-flat-transitive`). The map `P → D` is finite, generated by `1`,
   and finitely presented, with no algebra generators and the chosen relations.
2. For each base piece `T = B, A', A`, right exactness
   (`lem-weil-pbc-tensor-right-exact`) makes `P_T → D_T` surjective. Its kernel
   is generated by the images of the chosen relations: expand each element of
   the original ideal in those generators and use pure tensor generation
   (`def-weil-pbc-module-tensor-product`). Thus each map is finite and finitely
   presented (`def-weil-pbc-finitely-presented-algebra`).
3. Restricting scalars along these maps preserves finite presentation of `N`
   and `M'` by `lem-trf-finite-extension-module-finite-presentation`. Their base
   flatness is unchanged. The gluing equivalence restricts to a `P_A`-linear one.
4. Apply `lem-sfb-relative-fp-module-fibre-product` with flat ambient algebra `P`.
   The same compatible-pair module is finitely presented over `P`.
5. Its `P`-action is the restriction of its coordinatewise `D`-action. Apply the
   reverse direction of `lem-trf-finite-extension-module-finite-presentation`
   along `P → D` to conclude finite presentation over `D`.
-/
theorem finitePresentation_relative_fpAlgebra_fibreProduct
    {A : Type uA} {A' : Type uA'} {B : Type uB}
    [CommRing A] [CommRing A'] [CommRing B]
    (f : B →+* A) (g : A' →+* A) (hg : Function.Surjective g)
    [Algebra (f.pullback g) B] [Algebra (f.pullback g) A']
    [Algebra (f.pullback g) A]
    (hB : algebraMap (f.pullback g) B = f.pullbackFst g)
    (hA' : algebraMap (f.pullback g) A' = f.pullbackSnd g)
    (hA : algebraMap (f.pullback g) A = f.comp (f.pullbackFst g))
    (D : Type uD) [CommRing D] [Algebra (f.pullback g) D]
    (E : Type uE) [CommRing E] [Algebra (f.pullback g) E] [Algebra E D]
    [IsScalarTower (f.pullback g) E D]
    [Module.Flat (f.pullback g) E] [Algebra.FinitePresentation E D]
    [Algebra B (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B)]
    [Algebra A' (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A')]
    (hDB : ∀ b : B, algebraMap B (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) b = 1 ⊗ₜ b)
    (hDA' : ∀ a' : A', algebraMap A' (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') a' = 1 ⊗ₜ a')
    [Algebra (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A)]
    [Algebra (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A)]
    (hBA : ∀ (s : D) (b : B),
      algebraMap (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A) (s ⊗ₜ b) =
        s ⊗ₜ f b)
    (hA'A : ∀ (s : D) (a' : A'),
      algebraMap (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A) (s ⊗ₜ a') =
        s ⊗ₜ g a')
    [IsScalarTower D (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A)]
    [IsScalarTower D (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A)]
    (N : Type uN) [AddCommGroup N] [Module (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) N]
    [Module B N] [IsScalarTower B (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) N]
    [Module D N] [IsScalarTower D (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) N]
    [Module.FinitePresentation (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) N] [Module.Flat B N]
    (M' : Type uM) [AddCommGroup M'] [Module (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') M']
    [Module A' M'] [IsScalarTower A' (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') M']
    [Module D M'] [IsScalarTower D (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') M']
    [Module.FinitePresentation (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') M'] [Module.Flat A' M']
    (φ : ((D ⊗[f.pullback g] A) ⊗[D ⊗[f.pullback g] B] N) ≃ₗ[D ⊗[f.pullback g] A]
      ((D ⊗[f.pullback g] A) ⊗[D ⊗[f.pullback g] A'] M')) :
    Module.FinitePresentation D
      (LinearMap.ker
        (((φ.toLinearMap.restrictScalars D) ∘ₗ
          (LinearMap.restrictScalars D
            (TensorProduct.mk (D ⊗[f.pullback g] B) (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A) N 1))) ∘ₗ
            LinearMap.fst D N M' -
          (LinearMap.restrictScalars D
            (TensorProduct.mk (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A') (D ⊗[f.pullback g] A) M' 1)) ∘ₗ
              LinearMap.snd D N M')) := by
  sorry

end Module
